\subtree[designs-documents]{
\title{The full design documents}

\p{The long documents of the design phase, moved into the forest as they were written. The notes above state the point of each part and cite these for the detail.}

\ul{
\li{[The instruction set of the machine](design-isa-document), with its as-built notes.}
\li{[The reconciliation of the design review](design-reconciliation-document), whose errata correct the instruction set.}
\li{[The architecture document](design-architecture-document): the export reader, the stores, the reference engine, the driver and the build.}
\li{[The value model, second version](design-values-v2-document): the full text of the design with its prototype; a draft.}
\li{[The switches of the machine and the default configuration](design-switches-document): the one list, with the gates and measurements of the default set.}
\li{[The platform document](design-platform-document): JVM launcher against native image, collectors and heap settings, with the measurement tables.}
}
}
